ok - the sandbox gets only the clone, task directories and read-only brief, and is removed on exit
ok - only allowlisted variables reach the sandbox
ok - the commit identity the clone carries also reaches the sandbox environment
ok - a GitHub token is stored as a per-sandbox secret and never appears in argv or the environment
ok - without a token or allow list the sandbox gets neither a secret nor a network rule
ok - a symlinked token file is never read
ok - a no-mistakes ship gets the in-VM pipeline, its network, and a final sync
ok - origin is fetched, its default branch set and the pipeline initialised before claude starts
ok - the host gh is installed for a no-mistakes ship and an unusable copy is dropped
ok - a fork ship starts with the fork-only token and an origin that is the fork, without anyone swapping them
ok - the swap applies to a ship of the Firstmate fork only and leaves the home's token for everything else
ok - an absent, symlinked or empty fork token leaves the sandbox on the home's token with a notice
ok - an explicit FM_SBX_GH_TOKEN is never replaced by the fork token
ok - a no-mistakes ship gets the host's pinned ShellCheck and actionlint inside the sandbox
ok - a host tool at another version, absent or unable to run is never installed and the lint step still fails naming it
ok - a VM copy that differs from the host, or a host that differs from the pin, refuses before the worker starts
ok - a failed in-VM init stops the launch and removes the sandbox
ok - a missing host no-mistakes refuses and leaves no sandbox
ok - an npm seed cache is mounted read-only with offline settings, and only when given
ok - only this home's own hooks directory is mounted
ok - the brief's status and worktree paths resolve inside the VM
ok - malformed or unsafe arguments refuse before any sandbox is created
ok - a stopped daemon refuses
ok - a failed create stops the launch
ok - TERM and HUP each remove the sandbox before the wrapper exits
ok - a ship's commits reach the host worktree repository when the wrapper exits
ok - --verify mounts the spool and result directory and names the spool
ok - without --verify the run is exactly as before
ok - a bad or missing verification setup refuses before the sandbox is created
ok - terminating a verifying sandbox stops the broker with a forced emulator shutdown
ok - the local profile gets its environment, a sandbox-scoped rule and the spawn's claim for the worker's life
ok - without --local-llm nothing local is added
ok - a down server refuses before a sandbox exists and releases the slot
ok - a wrapper that fails its preflight releases the spawn's claim
ok - a wrapper without its own spawn's claim is refused before a sandbox exists
ok - a sandbox that can still reach the Anthropic API stops the launch and is removed
ok - a VM that cannot reach the server stops the launch and removes the sandbox
